RAMSES parameter file -- LEVITATING GAS, CALIMA + DUST DYNAMICS -- SMOKE TEST (production settings, reduced size)

The Krumholz & Thompson (2013) / Davis et al. (2014) dusty atmosphere as run by
Rosdahl & Teyssier 2015 (RT15) sec. 3.7, modelled on patch/rt/davis/davis.nml.

RT15's dimensional setup is matched EXACTLY in both folders:

                          RT15         here
    F_*                1.03e4       1.03e4        erg/cm2/s
    T_*                82           82            K
    g                  1.46e-6      1.46e-6       cm/s2
    rho_*              7.1e-16      7.1e-16       g/cm3
    kappa_R,*          2.13         2.1248        cm2/g_gas
    c_*                0.54         0.5390        km/s     (derived)
    h_* = c_iso^2/g    2e15         1.9897e15     cm       (derived)
    t_* = h_*/c_*      3.67e10      3.6916e10     s        (derived)
    Sigma = rho_* h_*  1.4          1.4127        g/cm2    (derived)
    tau_* = kappa Sigma  3          3.0017                 (derived)
    f_E,* = kappa F/(cg) 0.5        0.5000                 (derived)

Units are units_length = h_*, units_time = t_*, units_density = rho_*, so
g = 1, d_region = 1, p_region = 1 and Sigma = 1 in code units -- the same
normalisation as davis.nml (gravity_params = 0,-1).

THIS FOLDER: identical physics, but compiled with CALIMA (RTZ = 1, CALIMA = 1,
NDUST = 1, NPAH = 0) and with the dust treated as a DRIFTING fluid:

    dust_tva         = .true.   gas drag (terminal velocity approximation)
    dust_radpressure = .true.   radiation pressure on the dust

EVERY other dust process is off -- growth, coagulation, shattering, sputtering,
sublimation, SN destruction/injection, RATD, collisional cooling,
photoelectric heating, the turbulent subgrid model. They all default to .false.
in calima/dust_commons.f90, so this namelist simply does not switch them on.
One bin, one chemical type, pure graphite at 0.01 um.

Matched opacity: CALIMA takes the IR Rosseland mean from the grain optics rather
than from a T^2 law, giving 129.881 cm2 per gram of DUST at 82 K. The dust-to-gas
ratio in dustylevatm_condinit is therefore set to eps = 0.016359, which makes
kappa per gram of GAS equal 2.1248 cm2/g -- exactly RT15's kappa_R,*. So this
run has RT15's ENTIRE dimensional setup, and the only differences from the
reference folder are the temperature dependence of kappa and the dust dynamics.

The gas opacity is zero by construction: the single group is the far-IR band
(0.001-0.1 eV), below every ionisation threshold RTZ tracks, and
photoionisation is off in the network. Note rt_init RECOMPUTES group_egy for
that band as 6.696e-2 eV, so rt_n_bound below is F_* divided by THAT, not by
the namelist group_egy.

SMOKE TEST. Identical to the production namelist EXCEPT: 64^2 over 32 h_*
(same dy = 0.5 h_* as production), tend = 3 t_*, and rt_c_ramp_nstep = 300 so
the light-speed ramp completes inside the run and both branches of
rt_ramp_lightspeed are exercised. Everything else -- the full-c ramp start,
the emitting bottom boundary, the opacity switches, the group settings and
(folder B) the dust dynamics -- is exactly the production configuration.
Purpose: confirm the production settings do not crash before spending
cluster time. For reference, the production namelist is RT15's resolution: 2048^2 over L_box = 1024 h_*, 200 t_*,
and the light-speed ramp from full c over 3e4 RHD steps. It is a CLUSTER run --
the ramp alone is ~400x more expensive per unit physical time than running at
c_red (measured: 2.8 steps/min at 256^2 on 12 cores), which is exactly why RT15
needed 3e4 steps to cover 'the initial few t_*'. Use the _quick namelist locally.

Diagnostics (plot-levgas.py) reproduce RT15 figs. 9-11 and 13:
  f_E,V = <f_y,rad>/<g rho>                                     (eq. 84, 0.5 at t=0)
  tau_V = L_box <kappa_R rho>                                   (eq. 85, 3   at t=0)
  tau_F = L_box <kappa_R rho F_y>/<F_y>, plotted as tau_F/tau_V (eq. 86, 1   at t=0)
  f_y,rad = kappa_R rho F_y/c - (1/3) dE_t/dy                   (eq. 81)
plus rho/rho_* and T_rad/T_* projections at 25, 50, 75 and 150 t_* (fig. 10).

BOUNDARIES -- matched to patch/rt/davis
  x            periodic, matter and radiation
  bottom       reflective for matter; EMITS F_* for radiation via RT15 eq. 83,
               c~E_0 = F_* - F_y,1 + c~E_1, implemented in the local
               patch/rt_hydro_boundary.f90 (PATCH = patch in the Makefile).
               An rt_nsource region was tried and rejected: it imposes Np every
               RT subcycle and so also destroys returning radiation, collapsing
               the net injection to 18% of F_* once photons pile up.
  top          Dirichlet, rho = 1e-13 rho_*, v = 0, T = 1e3 T_*, zero radiation.
               NOTE RT15's text says T = 1e-3 T_*, but their
               hydro_boundary.f90 uses 1e3 T_*, and only that satisfies the
               "in pressure balance with the initial conditions" they also
               state: 1e-13 x 1e3 = 1e-10 = the initial density floor at T_*.

&RUN_PARAMS
hydro=.true.
rt=.true.
poisson=.true.
pic=.false.
static=.false.
nrestart=0
nremap=20
verbose=.false.
/

&AMR_PARAMS
levelmin=6
levelmax=6
ngridmax=20000
nparttot=1
nexpand=1
boxlen=32.0                  ! 32 h_*, 64^2 cells -> dy = 0.5 h_* = production
/

&POISSON_PARAMS
gravity_type=1
gravity_params=0.0,-1.0      ! g = c_iso^2/h_* = 1, along -y
/

&BOUNDARY_PARAMS
nboundary=2
jbound_min=-1,+1
jbound_max=-1,+1
bound_type= 1, 3             ! bottom mirror (+ emitting via the patch), top Dirichlet
d_bound  = 0.0, 1.0d-13
p_bound  = 0.0, 1.0d-10
u_bound  = 0.0, 0.0
v_bound  = 0.0, 0.0
/

&INIT_PARAMS
condinit_kind='dustylevatm'
nregion=1
region_type(1)='square'
exp_region(1)=10.0           ! max norm. With the DEFAULT exponent a "square"
                             ! region is an ELLIPSE and misses the corners in 2D.
x_center=16
y_center=16
length_x=64
length_y=64
d_region=1.0                 ! = rho_*
u_region=0.0
p_region=1.0                 ! p/d = c_iso^2 = 1
var_region(1,:)=0.0
/

&OUTPUT_PARAMS
noutput=5
tout = 0.0,0.5,1.0,2.0,3.0
tend = 3.0
/

&HYDRO_PARAMS
gamma=1.4
courant_factor=0.8
slope_type=1                 ! davis.nml
pressure_fix=.true.          ! davis.nml
beta_fix=0.5                 ! davis.nml
riemann='hllc'
data_dir = '/Users/currodri/Documents/RAMSES_dev/rtzdata_for_public_ramses/'
/

&COOLING_PARAMS
metal = .true. 
cooling = .false.
z_ave = 1.0d0                ! RT15's kappa carries no metallicity scaling
/

&REFINE_PARAMS
interpol_var=0
interpol_type=2
/

&UNITS_PARAMS
units_length  = 1.9897137d15      ! h_* = c_iso^2/g with RT15's g = 1.46e-6
units_time    = 3.6916359d10      ! t_* = h_*/c_*   (RT15 quote 3.67e10)
units_density = 7.1d-16           ! rho_*
/

&RT_PARAMS
rt_flux_scheme='glf'         ! mandatory for IR trapping (RT15 footnote 3)
rt_courant_factor=0.8
rt_c_fraction=3d-3           ! TARGET reduced light speed, as RT15
rt_c_ramp_start=1.0d0        ! start at the FULL c, as RT15
rt_c_ramp_nstep=300          ! shortened so the ramp COMPLETES inside this run
rt_otsa=.true.
rt_smooth=.true.             ! these four follow davis.nml
rt_vc=.true.
rt_T_rad=.false.
rt_pressBoost=1d0
rt_is_init_xion=.true.
rt_nsubcycle=4000
rt_isIR=.true.
rt_isIRtrap=.true.
!----------- F_* : emitting bottom boundary + RT15's initial field ----------!
rt_n_bound = 9.600888e+16, 1.0d-50
rt_nregion = 1
rt_region_type(1) = 'square'
rt_exp_region(1) = 10.0
rt_reg_x_center(1) = 16
rt_reg_y_center(1) = 16
rt_reg_length_x(1) = 64
rt_reg_length_y(1) = 64
rt_n_region(1) = 3.202511e+06
rt_v_region(1) = 3.202511e+06      ! = rt_n_region gives a fully directed beam, f = 1
rt_reg_group(1) = 1
rtz_cooling=.true.
rtz_include_collisional_ionization=.false.
rtz_include_photoionization=.false.
rtz_include_cosmic_ray_ionization=.false.
rtz_include_charge_exchange=.false.
rtz_include_dust_recombination=.false.
rtz_include_HM12_UVB=.false.
isH2_rtz=.false.
isCO_rtz=.false.
rtz_UV_background_G0=0.d0
rtz_max_cool_timestep=1.d20
rt_Tconst=82.0d0
/

&RT_GROUPS
! Far-IR band. group_egy is RECOMPUTED by rt_init for a CALIMA build.
group_egy     = 0.01
groupL0       = 0.001
groupL1       = 0.1
/

&CALIMA_PARAMS
dust_tva=.true.              ! gas drag
dust_radpressure=.true.      ! radiation pressure on the dust
use_w_drift_test=.false.
! One bin, one chemical type, pure graphite at 0.01 um. Every other dust
! process is left at its .false. default (see calima/dust_commons.f90).
dust_composition(1,6) = 1d0
dustbins_per_chemtype=1
asize=0.01d0                 ! must match averaged_cross_section_DustBin_01.txt
sgrain=2.2d0
amin = 3d-3
amax = 3d-2
charging_model='RM2026'
dust_tables_dir='/Users/currodri/Documents/RAMSES_dev/rtzdata_for_public_ramses/calima_data/'
/
